# Provenance of vendor/carve-grammars
#
# This directory is a COPY of markup-carve/carve-grammars, not an installed
# package: package.json resolves it as `file:./vendor/carve-grammars`. Until
# this file existed there was no record of which commit was copied, so the only
# available reading of `"version": "0.3.0"` in the vendored package.json was
# that it named a release neither npm nor Packagist has ever carried
# (carve#735).
#
# Recovered by blob identity rather than by trusting any label: nineteen of the
# twenty-three vendored files are byte-identical to carve-grammars
# 43272cc64d4d, and tiptap/serializer.js matches that commit and NO OTHER commit in
# the repository's history, which fixes the snapshot exactly. `0.3.0` turns out
# not to be a fiction at all - it is what carve-grammars itself declared at the
# time; upstream later LOWERED its version to 0.1.2, which is why the number
# looks impossible from today.
#
# The remaining four files are deliberate local edits on top of that snapshot,
# and none of them matches any upstream commit:
#
#   package.json    the scoped name `@markup-carve/carve-grammars`, adopted
#                   here before upstream did (carve-grammars#41)
#   README.md       an older, shorter inline-syntax table
#   carve-footnote.js, carve-footnote-definition.js
#                   parseHTML priority 60, so a footnote ref is not claimed by
#                   the Superscript mark and a labelled footnote `li` is not
#                   claimed by ListItem. Both carry a `[carve-wysiwyg vendor
#                   patch]` comment in place.
#
# engine-drift.yml reads every line below. `verbatim` files must still equal
# upstream at the recorded commit; `local` files must still equal the recorded
# hash, so a silent edit cannot hide behind the word "local"; and the file list
# must match the directory exactly, so adding a file cannot slip past unrecorded.
#
# Regenerate with: node tools/record-vendor-provenance.mjs <carve-grammars checkout>

